title: t/containers.t removes its container twice on live runs
updated: 2026-08-25T13:48:51Z
---

The live path registers a cleanup at line 84 and also removes the container at line 108, so every live run prints "Cleanup failed: ... no such container". Harmless -- the END block evals it -- but it is noise on every live run and trains the reader to ignore cleanup warnings. Make the registered cleanup tolerant of an already-removed container, or drop the explicit removal.

Committed; verified live against the podman socket - zero cleanup warnings, suite 102 PASS.
